0 76 549 [
[(Amplitudes of audio signals can have any reasonable range,)]
[(but when you output a signal via the [dac~] object, the)]
[(samples should range between -1 and +1. Values out of that)]
[(range will be "clipped".)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 61 80 [
[(Pd assumes you have a two channel audio system unless you tell it)]
[(otherwise. The [dac~] object, by default, connects to these two)]
[(channels.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo-Regular findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 61 177 [
[(Here we calculate a gain for the multiplier [*~] using a [dbtorms])]
[(object \050acronym for "dB to RMS"\051. 100 dB is normalized to one, and)]
[(zero dB artificially outputs a true 0 amplitude. Hence, decibels in)]
[(Pd are basically dBFS with an offset of 100! The dBFS is usually)]
[(considered in digital systems and 0 dB corresponds to one, whereas a)]
[(true zero amplitude value consists of minus infinity dB.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
